From 007eab9c6a06b8b2a540ac9033988804003cfe4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:05:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): interrupt and carry background reviews so a busy
 session no longer blocks a core update [daveey]

A background review holds an admission reservation for its whole run and read the drain's pause request
only between provider calls, so one long call kept the reservation past the drain's claim hold and the
update deferred 60 minutes (a laptop: "admission reservations busy (1)", one
background_review of a Desktop session that reviews after nearly every turn).

- Each review's watcher interrupts its in-flight call once a pause request has stood 5 s
  (REVIEW_UPDATE_PAUSE_GRACE_S); the review releases its reservation and is requeued as before.
- A review the update's admission hold refuses at spawn is queued (bounded) instead of dropped.
- Requeued reviews are also recorded per session on disk (agent/review_update_carry.py), so the
  session's next finished turn after the update's restart runs the review; a review that starts clears it.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
